[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138092,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Nodular hyperplasia of the ciliary epithelium is a well-circumscribed proliferation of the inner non-pigmented epithelium of the pars plicata of the ciliary body not associated with injury.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138093,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138094,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9A90.Y Other specified degeneration of iris or ciliary body</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138095,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable: </em>adenomatous hyperplasia of the ciliary body; Fuchs adenoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> coronal adenoma; age-related hyperplasia of the non-pigmented ciliary body epithelium; pseudoadenomatous hyperplasia of the ciliary body epithelium.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:08"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138096,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138097,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperplasia of the ciliary epithelium is located in the pars plicata of the ciliary body and is usually confined to a single ciliary process.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138098,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperplasia of the ciliary epithelium is typically an incidental finding in an enucleated eye, because it is generally small and asymptomatic. It can be imaged by ultrasound biomicroscopy {32830591}. It can occasionally cause a sectoral cataract or grow to sufficient size to involve the iris root. Rarely, a larger hyperplasia may mimic a malignant tumour of the ciliary body {32434227}. These lesions can be solitary or multiple and unilateral or bilateral.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138099,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperplasia of the ciliary epithelium is associated with age. At autopsy, these lesions are found in only about 5% of eyes from individuals &lt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;years of age, but in about 60% of eyes from individuals &gt;&nbsp;80&nbsp;years {25545484}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138100,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperplasia of the ciliary epithelium is an age-related degenerative lesion.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138101,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This type of hyperplasia of the ciliary epithelium results in a nodular growth pattern. It appears to be associated with ageing. No genetic profile has been published.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138102,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperplasias of the ciliary epithelium appear as small, yellowish-white or slightly pigmented nodules in a single ciliary process in the pars plicata of the ciliary body.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138103,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperplasia of the ciliary epithelium forms a small nodule that is composed of interlacing cords of uniform non-pigmented ciliary epithelial cells, surrounded by amorphous extracellular hyaline material that stains with PAS. The nodules may be pedunculated, countersunk, or embedded in the stroma of the ciliary body. In some cases, the extracellular material may be the predominant feature, with only occasional strands of epithelial cells. The extracellular material is immunoreactive for collagen&nbsp;IV and laminin {25545484}. Immunoreactivity for vimentin is reported {12180792}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 138104,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 112,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:01:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
